Evaluate on held-out data or an appropriate time-based split.
Display feature explanations only when the model and available data support them.
Disable or label the model as unavailable when there is insufficient training data.

Do not claim that a model is accurate merely because it produces a prediction.

8. What about existing energy-analysis tools?

Your literature review focuses on research papers, but a stronger comparison should also consider established tools and methodologies.

For example, the U.S. Department of Energy provides a Home Energy Score methodology that considers climate when comparing homes. Its Building Energy Data program also addresses data standards and the organization of building-energy information.

